        <mxCell id="legend" value="RELATIONSHIP KEY&#10;Each child references exactly one parent.&#10;Each parent may have zero or many children.&#10;All domain foreign keys use ON DELETE CASCADE.&#10;&#10;COLUMN KEY&#10;PK = primary key; FK = foreign key&#10;NN = NOT NULL; unmarked columns allow NULL&#10;GEN = generated column; IDENTITY columns are NN." style="rounded=0;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#F3F6F4;strokeColor=#B1C7BF;strokeWidth=1.6;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#203A36;fontStyle=0;spacing=12;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="40" y="1010" width="570" height="270" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="erd-notes" value="SCHEMA NOTES&#10;Composite activity FK prevents a zone from another project being referenced. GiST index supports zone geometry; other indexes support project/date and measurement history reads. Area and layer volume are query results, not stored columns.&#10;&#10;The migration runner also creates schema_migrations(name PK, applied_at). It is an operational ledger, outside the four domain tables. No users, sensors, soil batches, rule versions or attachment tables exist in this schema." style="rounded=0;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#F3F6F4;strokeColor=#B1C7BF;strokeWidth=1.6;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#203A36;fontStyle=0;spacing=12;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
